// Module 9: Volumes by slicing, disks, washers and shells

export default {
  id: 'volumes',
  number: 9,
  part: 'applications',
  hw: 'HW1',
  title: 'Volumes by slicing, disks and shells',
  summary: 'Volume as the integral of cross-sectional area, V = ∫ A(x) dx; solids of revolution by disks, washers and cylindrical shells; choosing the method; derivations of the cone and sphere formulas. MATLAB: volume integrals with integral() and plots of the generating region.',
  intro: String.raw`<p>Slice a solid into thin slabs. A slab at position $x$ with cross-sectional area $A(x)$ and thickness $\mathrm d x$ has volume $A(x)\,\mathrm d x$, and adding the slabs gives $V = \int_a^b A(x)\,\mathrm d x$. For solids of revolution the slices are disks or washers, or — slicing the other way — thin cylindrical shells. Homework 1 asks you to <i>derive</i> volume formulas in this way, so every result here is written as a derivation.</p>`,
  lessons: [
    {
      id: 'slicing',
      title: 'Volume by slicing',
      blocks: [
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>Rotating the region under $y = \sqrt x$, $0 \le x \le 4$, about the $x$-axis gives a paraboloid. Move the slice and increase the number of slabs: each slab is a thin cylinder, and the sum of their volumes approaches the volume of the solid — a Riemann sum for $\int_0^4 A(x)\,\mathrm d x$.</p>` },
        { type: 'widget', name: 'solid', config: {
          title: 'Slicing a paraboloid: y = √x rotated about the x-axis',
          f: 'sqrt(x)', a: 0, b: 4, method: 'disk', volumeTex: String.raw`8\pi`,
        } },
        { type: 'callout', kind: 'def', title: 'Volume by cross-sections', html: String.raw`<p>If a solid lies between the planes $x = a$ and $x = b$ and its cross-section perpendicular to the $x$-axis at $x$ has area $A(x)$ (continuous), then</p>$$V = \int_a^b A(x)\,\mathrm d x .$$<p>Two solids with equal cross-sectional areas at every height have equal volumes (Cavalieri's principle).</p>` },
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p><b>Example.</b> The base of a solid is the disc $x^2 + y^2 \le r^2$. Each cross-section perpendicular to the $x$-axis is a square with one side in the base. We find the side length at position $x$, then the area of the square, then add up the slices.</p>` },
        { type: 'derive', symbolic: true, title: 'A solid with square cross-sections on a disc', colors: { r: 1, s: 2, A: 3, F: 4 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Side = top of the chord − bottom of the chord',
            from: String.raw`s(x)=\T{yt-1}{\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}-\left(\T{yb-1}{-\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}\right)`,
            to: String.raw`s(x)=\T{s-1}{2\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}`, map: { 'yt-1': ['s-1'], 'yb-1': ['s-1'] },
            why: String.raw`At position $x$ the chord of the disc runs from $y=-\sqrt{r^2-x^2}$ up to $y=\sqrt{r^2-x^2}$. Subtracting a negative number adds it, so the length is twice the root.` },
          { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Put the side into $A = s^2$`,
            from: String.raw`A(x)=s(x)^2\qquad s(x)=\T{s-1}{2\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}`,
            to: String.raw`A(x)=\left(\T{s-1}{2\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}\right)^2`, arrows: { 's-1': 'insert s(x)' },
            why: String.raw`A cross-section is a square, and the area of a square is its side squared.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square both factors',
            to: String.raw`A(x)=\T{A-1}{4\left(r^2-x^2\right)}`, map: { 's-1': ['A-1'] },
            why: String.raw`$(2\sqrt w)^2 = 2^2\cdot(\sqrt w)^2 = 4w$: squaring undoes the square root, because $r^2-x^2 \ge 0$ on the disc.` },
          { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Add up the slices: $V=\int_{-r}^{r}A(x)\,\mathrm dx$`,
            from: String.raw`V=\int_{-r}^{r}A(x)\,\mathrm dx\qquad A(x)=\T{A-1}{4\left(r^2-x^2\right)}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\int_{-r}^{r}\T{A-1}{4\left(r^2-x^2\right)}\,\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'A-1': 'slice area' },
            why: String.raw`A slab of thickness $\mathrm dx$ has volume $A(x)\,\mathrm dx$. The solid reaches from $x=-r$ to $x=r$.` },
          { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
            to: String.raw`V=4\Big[\T{F-1}{r^2x-\frac{x^3}{3}}\Big]_{-r}^{r}`, map: { 'A-1': ['F-1'] },
            why: String.raw`The constant $4$ stays in front. $r^2$ does not depend on $x$, so its antiderivative is $r^2x$; the antiderivative of $x^2$ is $\frac{x^3}{3}$.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Upper limit minus lower limit`,
            to: String.raw`V=4\left(\T{up-1}{r^3-\frac{r^3}{3}}-\left(\T{lo-1}{-r^3+\frac{r^3}{3}}\right)\right)`, map: { 'F-1': ['up-1', 'lo-1'] }, arrows: { 'F-1': 'x = r, then x = −r' },
            why: String.raw`Insert $x=r$, then $x=-r$, and subtract the second value from the first.` },
          { kind: 'result', label: 'Simplify',
            to: String.raw`V=4\cdot\T{F-2}{\frac{4r^3}{3}}=\frac{16r^3}{3}`, map: { 'up-1': ['F-2'], 'lo-1': ['F-2'] },
            why: String.raw`The upper value is $\frac{2r^3}{3}$ and the lower value is $-\frac{2r^3}{3}$; subtracting a negative doubles it to $\frac{4r^3}{3}$. Times $4$ gives the volume.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'derive', title: 'With numbers: a disc of radius 3 cm', given: String.raw`\T{r-0}{r}=3\text{ cm}`, colors: { r: 1, s: 2, A: 3, F: 4 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radius into the formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\frac{16\,\T{r-x}{r}^3}{3}\qquad r=\T{r-1}{3}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{16\cdot\T{r-1}{3}^3}{3}`, arrows: { 'r-1': 'r = 3 cm' },
            why: String.raw`The number keeps the colour of the letter it replaces.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$3^3 = 27$, then $27 \div 3 = 9$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{16\cdot\T{r-1}{27}}{3}=16\cdot 9=144\text{ cm}^3`,
            why: String.raw`The radius is in cm, so $r^3$ is in $\text{cm}^3$, a volume.` },
          { kind: 'check', label: 'Check with the integral itself',
            from: String.raw`V=\int_{-3}^{3}4\left(9-x^2\right)\mathrm dx`,
            to: String.raw`V=4\Big[9x-\frac{x^3}{3}\Big]_{-3}^{3}=4\big(18-(-18)\big)=144\text{ cm}^3\ \checkmark`,
            why: String.raw`Integrating the slice areas directly with $r=3$ gives the same 144 cm³, so the formula is right.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'quiz', question: String.raw`A pyramid has a square base of side $a$ and height $h$. At height $z$ the cross-section is a square of side $a(1 - z/h)$. Its volume is …`, choices: [String.raw`$a^2 h$`, String.raw`$\frac{a^2 h}{2}$`, String.raw`$\frac{a^2 h}{3}$`, String.raw`$\frac{a^2 h}{4}$`], answer: 2, explain: String.raw`$V = \int_0^h a^2\left(1 - \frac zh\right)^2\mathrm d z = a^2\cdot\frac h3$ (substitute $u = 1 - z/h$).` },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'disks-washers',
      title: 'Solids of revolution: disks and washers',
      blocks: [
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>Rotating the graph of $y = R(x) \ge 0$ about the $x$-axis makes every cross-section a <b>disk</b> of radius $R(x)$, so $A(x) = \pi R(x)^2$. The upper half-circle $y = \sqrt{4 - x^2}$ generates a ball of radius 2:</p>` },
        { type: 'widget', name: 'solid', config: {
          title: 'Disk method: the ball of radius 2',
          f: 'sqrt(4 - x.^2)', a: -2, b: 2, method: 'disk', volumeTex: String.raw`\frac{32\pi}{3}`,
        } },
        { type: 'callout', kind: 'thm', title: 'Disk and washer formulas (rotation about the x-axis)', html: String.raw`$$V_{\text{disk}} = \pi\int_a^b R(x)^2\,\mathrm d x, \qquad V_{\text{washer}} = \pi\int_a^b \left(R(x)^2 - r(x)^2\right)\mathrm d x .$$<p>$R$ is the outer and $r$ the inner radius, both measured from the <b>axis of rotation</b>. For the axis $y = c$, use $R(x) = |f(x) - c|$. For rotation about the $y$-axis, slice perpendicular to it and integrate in $y$.</p>` },
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p><b>Cone.</b> A cone of height $h$ and base radius $r$ is generated by rotating the line $y = \frac{r}{h}x$, $0 \le x \le h$, about the $x$-axis: the line starts at the tip and reaches radius $r$ at $x = h$. The disk at $x$ has radius $R(x) = \frac{r x}{h}$.</p>` },
        { type: 'derive', symbolic: true, title: 'Derivation: volume of a cone', colors: { R: 1, r: 2, h: 3, x: 4 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radius into the disk formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^{h}R(x)^2\,\mathrm dx\qquad R(x)=\T{R-1}{\frac{r x}{h}}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^{h}\left(\T{R-1}{\frac{r x}{h}}\right)^2\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'R(x) = rx/h' },
            why: String.raw`Each slice is a disk of radius $R(x)$ and thickness $\mathrm dx$, so its volume is $\pi R(x)^2\,\mathrm dx$. The cone runs from the tip $x=0$ to the base $x=h$.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square the fraction',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^{h}\frac{\T{r-1}{r^2}\,\T{x-1}{x^2}}{\T{h-1}{h^2}}\,\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-1': ['r-1', 'x-1', 'h-1'] },
            why: String.raw`Squaring a fraction squares the top and the bottom: $\left(\frac{rx}{h}\right)^2 = \frac{r^2x^2}{h^2}$.` },
          { kind: 'factor', label: 'Constants out of the integral',
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{\pi\,\T{r-1}{r^2}}{\T{h-1}{h^2}}\int_0^{h}\T{x-1}{x^2}\,\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'r-1': 'constant: out front', 'h-1': '' },
            why: String.raw`$r$ and $h$ are fixed numbers for a given cone; only $x$ changes along the axis. Constant factors can be taken outside the integral.` },
          { kind: 'calculus', label: String.raw`Integrate $x^2$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{\pi\,\T{r-1}{r^2}}{\T{h-1}{h^2}}\Big[\T{F-1}{\frac{x^3}{3}}\Big]_0^{h}`, map: { 'x-1': ['F-1'] },
            why: String.raw`The antiderivative of $x^2$ is $\frac{x^3}{3}$.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Insert the limits $h$ and $0$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{\pi\,\T{r-1}{r^2}}{\T{h-1}{h^2}}\cdot\frac{\T{h-2}{h^3}}{3}`, map: { 'F-1': ['h-2'] },
            why: String.raw`At $x=h$ we get $\frac{h^3}{3}$, at $x=0$ we get $0$.` },
          { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$\frac{h^3}{h^2} = h$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac13\pi\,\T{r-1}{r^2}\,\T{h-2}{h}`,
            why: String.raw`Two of the three factors $h$ on top cancel against $h^2$ below. The cone is exactly one third of the cylinder $\pi r^2 h$ around it.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'derive', title: 'With numbers: a cone with r = 3 cm and h = 4 cm', given: String.raw`\T{r-0}{r}=3\text{ cm},\quad \T{h-0}{h}=4\text{ cm}`, colors: { R: 1, r: 2, h: 3, x: 4 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the given values into the formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\frac13\pi\,\T{r-x}{r}^2\,\T{h-x}{h}\qquad r=\T{r-1}{3},\quad h=\T{h-1}{4}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac13\pi\cdot\T{r-1}{3}^2\cdot\T{h-1}{4}`, arrows: { 'r-1': 'r = 3 cm', 'h-1': 'h = 4 cm' },
            why: String.raw`Each number keeps the colour of the letter it replaces.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$3^2 = 9$, then $\frac13\cdot 9\cdot 4 = 12$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac13\pi\cdot\T{r-1}{9}\cdot\T{h-1}{4}=12\pi\approx 37.7\text{ cm}^3`,
            why: String.raw`$\text{cm}^2\cdot\text{cm} = \text{cm}^3$, a volume.` },
          { kind: 'check', label: 'Check with the disk integral',
            from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^{4}\left(\frac{3x}{4}\right)^2\mathrm dx`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac{9\pi}{16}\Big[\frac{x^3}{3}\Big]_0^{4}=\frac{9\pi}{16}\cdot\frac{64}{3}=12\pi\ \checkmark`,
            why: String.raw`Integrating the disks for this cone directly gives the same $12\pi$.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p><b>Ball.</b> A ball of radius $r$ is generated by rotating the upper half-circle $y = \sqrt{r^2 - x^2}$, $-r \le x \le r$, about the $x$-axis.</p>` },
        { type: 'derive', symbolic: true, title: 'Derivation: volume of a ball', colors: { R: 1, A: 2, F: 3 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radius into the disk formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-r}^{r}R(x)^2\,\mathrm dx\qquad R(x)=\T{R-1}{\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-r}^{r}\left(\T{R-1}{\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}\right)^2\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'R(x)' },
            why: String.raw`The disk at $x$ has radius equal to the height of the half-circle there.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square and root cancel',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-r}^{r}\T{A-1}{\left(r^2-x^2\right)}\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-1': ['A-1'] },
            why: String.raw`$(\sqrt w)^2 = w$ for $w \ge 0$, and $r^2-x^2 \ge 0$ on $[-r, r]$.` },
          { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\Big[\T{F-1}{r^2x-\frac{x^3}{3}}\Big]_{-r}^{r}`, map: { 'A-1': ['F-1'] },
            why: String.raw`$r^2$ is a constant, so its antiderivative is $r^2x$; that of $x^2$ is $\frac{x^3}{3}$.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Upper limit minus lower limit',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\left(\T{up-1}{\frac{2r^3}{3}}-\left(\T{lo-1}{-\frac{2r^3}{3}}\right)\right)`, map: { 'F-1': ['up-1', 'lo-1'] }, arrows: { 'F-1': 'x = r, then x = −r' },
            why: String.raw`At $x=r$: $r^3-\frac{r^3}{3}=\frac{2r^3}{3}$. At $x=-r$: $-r^3+\frac{r^3}{3}=-\frac{2r^3}{3}$.` },
          { kind: 'result', label: 'Subtracting a negative doubles',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\cdot\T{F-2}{\frac{4r^3}{3}}=\frac43\pi r^3`, map: { 'up-1': ['F-2'], 'lo-1': ['F-2'] },
            why: String.raw`$\frac{2r^3}{3}-\left(-\frac{2r^3}{3}\right)=\frac{4r^3}{3}$. This is the familiar ball formula.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'derive', title: 'With numbers: a ball of radius 3 cm', given: String.raw`\T{r-0}{r}=3\text{ cm}`, colors: { R: 1, A: 2, F: 3, r: 4 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radius into the formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\frac43\pi\,\T{r-x}{r}^3\qquad r=\T{r-1}{3}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac43\pi\cdot\T{r-1}{3}^3`, arrows: { 'r-1': 'r = 3 cm' },
            why: String.raw`The number keeps the colour of the letter it replaces.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$3^3 = 27$, then $\frac43\cdot 27 = 36$`,
            to: String.raw`V=\frac43\pi\cdot\T{r-1}{27}=36\pi\approx 113.1\text{ cm}^3`,
            why: String.raw`$27\div 3 = 9$ and $4\cdot 9 = 36$.` },
          { kind: 'check', label: 'Check with the disk integral',
            from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-3}^{3}\left(9-x^2\right)\mathrm dx`,
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\Big[9x-\frac{x^3}{3}\Big]_{-3}^{3}=\pi\big(18-(-18)\big)=36\pi\ \checkmark`,
            why: String.raw`Integrating the disks directly with $r=3$ gives the same $36\pi$.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>If the region does not touch the axis, each slice is a <b>washer</b> — a disk with a hole. Rotating the region between $y = x$ (outer) and $y = x^2$ (inner), $0 \le x \le 1$:</p>` },
        { type: 'widget', name: 'solid', config: {
          title: 'Washer method: region between y = x and y = x² about the x-axis',
          f: 'x', g: 'x.^2', a: 0, b: 1, method: 'washer', volumeTex: String.raw`\frac{2\pi}{15}`,
        } },
        { type: 'derive', title: 'Example: the washer solid above', colors: { R: 1, r: 2 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put both radii into the washer formula',
            from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(R(x)^2-r(x)^2\right)\mathrm dx\qquad R(x)=\T{R-1}{x},\quad r(x)=\T{r-1}{x^2}`,
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(\T{R-1}{x}^2-\left(\T{r-1}{x^2}\right)^2\right)\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'outer', 'r-1': 'inner' },
            why: String.raw`On $[0, 1]$ we have $x \ge x^2$, so $y=x$ is farther from the axis: it is the outer radius, $y=x^2$ the inner one.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square each radius',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(\T{R-2}{x^2}-\T{r-2}{x^4}\right)\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-1': ['R-2'], 'r-1': ['r-2'] },
            why: String.raw`$(x^2)^2 = x^4$: a power of a power multiplies the exponents.` },
          { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\Big[\T{R-3}{\frac{x^3}{3}}-\T{r-3}{\frac{x^5}{5}}\Big]_0^1`, map: { 'R-2': ['R-3'], 'r-2': ['r-3'] },
            why: String.raw`Power rule: raise the exponent by one and divide by the new exponent.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Insert $x = 1$ (at $x = 0$ both terms are $0$)`,
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\left(\T{R-4}{\frac13}-\T{r-4}{\frac15}\right)`, map: { 'R-3': ['R-4'], 'r-3': ['r-4'] },
            why: String.raw`$1^3 = 1^5 = 1$.` },
          { kind: 'result', label: 'Common denominator 15',
            to: String.raw`V=\pi\cdot\T{V-1}{\frac{5-3}{15}}=\frac{2\pi}{15}`, map: { 'R-4': ['V-1'], 'r-4': ['V-1'] },
            why: String.raw`$\frac13=\frac{5}{15}$ and $\frac15=\frac{3}{15}$.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'quiz', question: String.raw`Which integrand gives the volume of the washer solid above?`, choices: [String.raw`$\pi\left(x - x^2\right)^2$`, String.raw`$\pi\left(x^2 - x^4\right)$`, String.raw`$2\pi x\left(x - x^2\right)$`, String.raw`$\pi\left(x - x^2\right)$`], answer: 1, explain: String.raw`Washer area is $\pi R^2 - \pi r^2$, not $\pi(R - r)^2$. Option 3 is a shell integrand, which would describe rotation about the $y$-axis.` },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'shells',
      title: 'Cylindrical shells and choosing the method',
      blocks: [
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>Rotate the region under $y = 2x - x^2$, $0 \le x \le 2$, about the <b>$y$-axis</b>. Washers would need $x$ as a function of $y$ (two branches $x = 1 \pm \sqrt{1 - y}$). Instead, rotate each thin vertical strip: it sweeps out a thin cylindrical <b>shell</b> of radius $x$, height $f(x)$ and thickness $\mathrm d x$.</p>` },
        { type: 'widget', name: 'solid', config: {
          title: 'Shell method: y = 2x − x² rotated about the y-axis',
          f: '2*x - x.^2', a: 0, b: 2, method: 'shell', volumeTex: String.raw`\frac{8\pi}{3}`,
        } },
        { type: 'callout', kind: 'thm', title: 'Shell formula (rotation about the y-axis)', html: String.raw`<p>Unrolled, a shell is a thin plate of length $2\pi x$ (circumference), height $h(x)$ and thickness $\mathrm d x$:</p>$$V = 2\pi\int_a^b x\,h(x)\,\mathrm d x, \qquad 0 \le a < b .$$<p>For rotation about the line $x = c$, the radius is $|x - c|$. Between two curves, $h(x) = f(x) - g(x)$.</p>` },
        { type: 'derive', title: 'Example: the shell solid above', colors: { rad: 1, ht: 2, p: 3 }, steps: [
          { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put radius and height into the shell formula',
            from: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_0^2 \text{radius}\cdot\text{height}\,\mathrm dx\qquad \text{radius}=\T{rad-1}{x},\quad \text{height}=\T{ht-1}{2x-x^2}`,
            to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_0^2\T{rad-1}{x}\left(\T{ht-1}{2x-x^2}\right)\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'rad-1': 'radius', 'ht-1': 'height' },
            why: String.raw`The strip at $x$ is at distance $x$ from the $y$-axis (the radius) and reaches up to the curve (the height $2x-x^2$).` },
          { kind: 'expand', label: String.raw`Multiply $x$ into the bracket`,
            to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_0^2\left(\T{p-1}{2x^2}-\T{p-2}{x^3}\right)\mathrm dx`, map: { 'rad-1': ['p-1', 'p-2'], 'ht-1': ['p-1', 'p-2'] }, arrows: { 'rad-1': '× each term' },
            why: String.raw`$x\cdot 2x = 2x^2$ and $x\cdot(-x^2) = -x^3$. We expand so that each term can be integrated with the power rule.` },
          { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
            to: String.raw`V=2\pi\Big[\T{p-3}{\frac{2x^3}{3}}-\T{p-4}{\frac{x^4}{4}}\Big]_0^2`, map: { 'p-1': ['p-3'], 'p-2': ['p-4'] },
            why: String.raw`Power rule on each term.` },
          { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Insert $x = 2$ (at $x = 0$ both terms are $0$)`,
            to: String.raw`V=2\pi\left(\T{p-5}{\frac{16}{3}}-\T{p-6}{4}\right)`, map: { 'p-3': ['p-5'], 'p-4': ['p-6'] },
            why: String.raw`$\frac{2\cdot 8}{3}=\frac{16}{3}$ and $\frac{16}{4}=4$.` },
          { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$\frac{16}{3}-\frac{12}{3}=\frac43$`,
            to: String.raw`V=2\pi\cdot\T{p-7}{\frac43}=\frac{8\pi}{3}`, map: { 'p-5': ['p-7'], 'p-6': ['p-7'] },
            why: String.raw`Write $4$ as $\frac{12}{3}$ to subtract, then multiply by $2\pi$.` },
        ] },
        { type: 'table', head: ['Axis of rotation', 'Strips parallel to the axis', 'Strips perpendicular to the axis'], rows: [
          ['$x$-axis', String.raw`shells in $y$: $2\pi\int y\,\ell(y)\,\mathrm d y$`, String.raw`disks/washers in $x$: $\pi\int (R^2 - r^2)\,\mathrm d x$`],
          ['$y$-axis', String.raw`shells in $x$: $2\pi\int x\,h(x)\,\mathrm d x$`, String.raw`disks/washers in $y$: $\pi\int (R^2 - r^2)\,\mathrm d y$`],
        ] },
        { type: 'callout', kind: 'exam', title: 'Choosing the method', html: String.raw`<p>Use the method whose strips are described by <b>one</b> formula over the whole interval in the variable you can express easily. If the boundary is given as $y = f(x)$ and the axis is vertical, shells usually win; if the axis is horizontal, disks or washers. State the radius and the height (or the radii) in a sentence before integrating.</p>` },
        { type: 'quiz', question: String.raw`The region under $y = e^{-x^2}$, $0 \le x \le 1$, is rotated about the $y$-axis. What is the volume?`, choices: [String.raw`$\pi\left(1 - e^{-1}\right)$`, String.raw`$2\pi\left(1 - e^{-1}\right)$`, String.raw`$\pi\int_0^1 e^{-2x^2}\,\mathrm d x$`, String.raw`$\frac{\pi}{2}\left(1 - e^{-1}\right)$`], answer: 0, explain: String.raw`Shells: $2\pi\int_0^1 x e^{-x^2}\,\mathrm d x = 2\pi\Big[-\frac12 e^{-x^2}\Big]_0^1 = \pi\left(1 - e^{-1}\right)$. Option 3 is the disk method for the $x$-axis.` },
      ],
    },
  ],
  matlab: [
    {
      id: 'volume-integrals',
      title: 'Volume integrals in MATLAB',
      blocks: [
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>A volume is an ordinary definite integral, so <code>integral</code> checks it. Write the radius functions as anonymous functions and keep the formula visible in the code: <code>V = pi*integral(@(x) R(x).^2 - r(x).^2, a, b)</code>. Always plot the <b>generating region</b> together with the axis of rotation — it is the picture graders want to see.</p>` },
        { type: 'code', caption: 'Washer solid: region between y = x and y = x², rotated about the x-axis.', editable: true, code: `R = @(x) x;          % outer radius
r = @(x) x.^2;       % inner radius
V = pi*integral(@(x) R(x).^2 - r(x).^2, 0, 1)
fprintf('exact 2*pi/15 = %.6f\\n', 2*pi/15)
x = linspace(0, 1, 200);
fill([x fliplr(x)], [R(x) fliplr(r(x))], [0.75 0.85 1])
hold on
yline(0, 'k--')                  % axis of rotation
grid on; axis equal
title('Generating region')` },
        { type: 'table', head: ['Type', 'Result'], rows: [
          [String.raw`<code>V = \pi \int_a^b R(x)^2\,\mathrm d x</code>`, String.raw`$V = \pi \int_a^b R(x)^2\,\mathrm d x$`],
          [String.raw`<code>V = \pi \int_a^b \left( R(x)^2 - r(x)^2 \right)\mathrm d x</code>`, String.raw`$V = \pi \int_a^b \left( R(x)^2 - r(x)^2 \right)\mathrm d x$`],
          [String.raw`<code>V = 2\pi \int_a^b x\,h(x)\,\mathrm d x</code>`, String.raw`$V = 2\pi \int_a^b x\,h(x)\,\mathrm d x$`],
        ] },
        { type: 'latex', prompt: 'Type the disk formula:', target: String.raw`V = \pi \int_a^b R(x)^2\,\mathrm d x` },
        { type: 'latex', prompt: 'Type the shell formula:', target: String.raw`V = 2\pi \int_a^b x\,h(x)\,\mathrm d x` },
        { type: 'matlab', prompt: String.raw`The region under $y = \sin x$, $0 \le x \le \pi$, is rotated about the $x$-axis. Store the volume in <code>V</code> (exact value $\pi^2/2$).`, starter: `R = @(x) sin(x);\nV = 0    % replace 0 by pi*integral(...)`, solution: `R = @(x) sin(x);\nV = pi*integral(@(x) R(x).^2, 0, pi)`, checks: [{ var: 'V', value: 'pi^2/2', tol: 1e-8 }, { uses: 'integral' }] },
        { type: 'matlab', prompt: String.raw`The same region is rotated about the $y$-axis. Use shells and store the volume in <code>Vs</code> (exact value $2\pi^2$). Plot the generating region with <code>fill</code>.`, starter: `h = @(x) sin(x);\nVs = 0    % replace 0 by 2*pi*integral(...)\nx = linspace(0, pi, 200);\n% fill(...)`, solution: `h = @(x) sin(x);\nVs = 2*pi*integral(@(x) x.*h(x), 0, pi)\nx = linspace(0, pi, 200);\nfill([x fliplr(x)], [h(x) 0*x], [0.8 0.9 1])\ngrid on`, checks: [{ var: 'Vs', value: '2*pi^2', tol: 1e-8 }, { uses: 'fill' }, { figure: true }], hint: String.raw`Shell integrand: <code>x.*h(x)</code> — element-wise product.` },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'volume-writeup',
      title: 'Writing a volume derivation',
      blocks: [
        { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>A derivation problem ("show that the volume is …") is answered with symbols, not numbers. The numerical check then picks sample values of the parameters and compares <code>integral</code> with the formula. The model below derives the volume of a <b>spherical cap</b> of height $h$ cut from a ball of radius $r$.</p>` },
        { type: 'livescript', caption: 'Model derivation: the spherical cap', blocks: [
          { type: 'heading', content: 'Problem 1 (Attempted)' },
          { type: 'text', content: 'We place the ball $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\le r^2$ so that the cap is the part with $y \\ge r - h$. The cross-section at height $y$ perpendicular to the $y$-axis is a disk of radius $\\sqrt{r^2 - y^2}$, so its area is' },
          { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`A(y) = \pi\left(r^2 - y^2\right).` },
          { type: 'text', content: 'We integrate the cross-sectional area over the height of the cap:' },
          { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`V = \pi \int_{r-h}^{r} \left(r^2 - y^2\right)\mathrm d y = \pi\Big[ r^2 y - \frac{y^3}{3} \Big]_{r-h}^{r} = \frac{\pi h^2 (3r - h)}{3}.` },
          { type: 'text', content: 'The last step is algebra: with $s = r - h$, $\\frac{2r^3}{3} - r^2 s + \\frac{s^3}{3} = \\frac{(r - s)^2(2r + s)}{3} = \\frac{h^2(3r - h)}{3}$. For $h = 2r$ we recover the ball $\\frac43\\pi r^3$. We check the formula for $r = 5$, $h = 2$ and plot the generating region:' },
          { type: 'code', content: "r = 5; h = 2;\nV = pi*integral(@(y) r^2 - y.^2, r - h, r)\nVformula = pi*h^2*(3*r - h)/3\ny = linspace(r - h, r, 200);\nfill([sqrt(r^2 - y.^2) 0*y], [y fliplr(y)], [0.75 0.85 1])\nhold on\nfplot(@(t) sqrt(r^2 - t.^2), [-r r]); xline(0, 'k--')\naxis equal; grid on" },
        ] },
        { type: 'latex', prompt: 'Type the cap integral:', target: String.raw`V = \pi \int_{r-h}^{r} \left(r^2 - y^2\right)\mathrm d y`, accept: [String.raw`V = \pi\int_{r-h}^{r}(r^2-y^2)\,dy`] },
        { type: 'callout', kind: 'exam', html: String.raw`<p>In a derivation, say where the solid sits in the coordinate system, which variable you integrate in, and what the radius (or area) of a slice is — <i>before</i> the integral appears.</p>` },
      ],
    },
  ],
  assignments: [
    {
      id: 'a1',
      title: 'Disks and washers',
      difficulty: 'core',
      statement: String.raw`<p>Find the volume of the solid obtained by rotating the region about the given axis.</p>`,
      parts: [
        { label: '(a)', prompt: String.raw`Under $y = e^x$, $0 \le x \le 1$, about the $x$-axis.`, kind: 'numeric', answer: 'pi*(exp(2) - 1)/2', solution: String.raw`$\pi\int_0^1 e^{2x}\,\mathrm d x = \frac{\pi(e^2 - 1)}{2}$.` },
        { label: '(b)', prompt: String.raw`Between $y = \sqrt x$ and $y = x$, about the $x$-axis.`, kind: 'numeric', answer: 'pi/6', solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>The curves meet at $x = 0$ and $x = 1$. On $[0, 1]$, $\sqrt x \ge x$, so $\sqrt x$ is the outer and $x$ the inner radius. We put both into the washer formula and integrate.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { R: 1, r: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radii into the washer formula',
              from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(R^2-r^2\right)\mathrm dx\qquad R=\T{R-1}{\sqrt x},\quad r=\T{r-1}{x}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(\left(\T{R-1}{\sqrt x}\right)^2-\T{r-1}{x}^2\right)\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'outer', 'r-1': 'inner' },
              why: String.raw`Washer area $=\pi R^2-\pi r^2$, both radii measured from the $x$-axis.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square each radius',
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^1\left(\T{R-2}{x}-\T{r-2}{x^2}\right)\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-1': ['R-2'], 'r-1': ['r-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$(\sqrt x)^2 = x$ for $x \ge 0$.` },
            { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\Big[\T{R-3}{\frac{x^2}{2}}-\T{r-3}{\frac{x^3}{3}}\Big]_0^1`, map: { 'R-2': ['R-3'], 'r-2': ['r-3'] },
              why: String.raw`Power rule on each term.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`Insert $x = 1$ and $x = 0$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\left(\T{R-4}{\frac12}-\T{r-4}{\frac13}\right)=\frac{\pi}{6}`, map: { 'R-3': ['R-4'], 'r-3': ['r-4'] },
              why: String.raw`At $x = 0$ both terms vanish; $\frac12-\frac13=\frac16$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(c)', prompt: String.raw`Between $y = x^2$ and $y = 4$, about the line $y = -1$.`, kind: 'numeric', answer: '1088*pi/15', hint: String.raw`Radii are distances to $y = -1$: $R = 5$, $r = x^2 + 1$.`, solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>The curves meet at $x = \pm 2$. Both radii are distances to the axis $y = -1$: the line $y = 4$ is $5$ away, the parabola is $x^2 + 1$ away. We put them into the washer formula, expand and integrate.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { R: 1, r: 2, c: 3, q: 4 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radii into the washer formula',
              from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-2}^{2}\left(R^2-r^2\right)\mathrm dx\qquad R=\T{R-1}{5},\quad r=\T{r-1}{x^2+1}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-2}^{2}\left(\T{R-1}{5}^2-\left(\T{r-1}{x^2+1}\right)^2\right)\mathrm dx`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'outer', 'r-1': 'inner' },
              why: String.raw`$R = 4-(-1) = 5$ and $r = x^2-(-1) = x^2+1$.` },
            { kind: 'expand', label: String.raw`Square: $(a+b)^2 = a^2+2ab+b^2$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-2}^{2}\left(\T{R-2}{25}-\left(\T{r-2}{x^4+2x^2+1}\right)\right)\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-1': ['R-2'], 'r-1': ['r-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$(x^2+1)^2 = x^4+2x^2+1$. Keep the bracket: the minus sign in front applies to all three terms.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Remove the bracket, $25-1=24$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{-2}^{2}\left(\T{c-1}{24}-\T{q-1}{2x^2}-\T{q-2}{x^4}\right)\mathrm dx`, map: { 'R-2': ['c-1'], 'r-2': ['c-1', 'q-1', 'q-2'] },
              why: String.raw`The minus sign flips every sign inside the bracket; the constants $25$ and $-1$ combine to $24$.` },
            { kind: 'factor', label: 'Even integrand: twice the integral over [0, 2]',
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_0^{2}\left(\T{c-1}{24}-\T{q-1}{2x^2}-\T{q-2}{x^4}\right)\mathrm dx`,
              why: String.raw`The integrand only contains even powers of $x$, so the part over $[-2, 0]$ equals the part over $[0, 2]$.` },
            { kind: 'calculus', label: String.raw`Integrate and insert $x = 2$`,
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\left(\T{c-2}{48}-\T{q-3}{\frac{16}{3}}-\T{q-4}{\frac{32}{5}}\right)`, map: { 'c-1': ['c-2'], 'q-1': ['q-3'], 'q-2': ['q-4'] },
              why: String.raw`The antiderivative is $24x-\frac{2x^3}{3}-\frac{x^5}{5}$; at $x=2$ it is $48-\frac{16}{3}-\frac{32}{5}$, at $x=0$ it is $0$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: 'Common denominator 15',
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\cdot\T{V-1}{\frac{720-80-96}{15}}=2\pi\cdot\frac{544}{15}=\frac{1088\pi}{15}`, map: { 'c-2': ['V-1'], 'q-3': ['V-1'], 'q-4': ['V-1'] },
              why: String.raw`$48=\frac{720}{15}$, $\frac{16}{3}=\frac{80}{15}$, $\frac{32}{5}=\frac{96}{15}$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'a2',
      title: 'Paraboloid bowl and spherical cap',
      difficulty: 'core',
      hw: 'HW1-style',
      statement: String.raw`<p>A bowl is obtained by rotating the curve $y = \frac49 x^2$, $0 \le x \le 3$, about the $y$-axis (units: dm). A second solid is a cap of height $h$ cut from a ball of radius $5$.</p>`,
      parts: [
        { label: '(a)', prompt: String.raw`Volume of water in the full bowl (depth $4$), in dm³:`, kind: 'numeric', answer: '18*pi', hint: String.raw`Disks in $y$: $x^2 = \frac{9y}{4}$.`, solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>The axis is the $y$-axis, so we slice horizontally: the water slice at height $y$ is a disk of radius $x$. We first solve the curve for $x^2$, then put it into the disk formula in $y$.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { x: 1, s: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'both', label: String.raw`Both sides $\times\frac94$`,
              from: String.raw`y=\frac49\,\T{x-1}{x^2}`,
              to: String.raw`\T{x-1}{x^2}=\frac94\,y`, arrows: { 'x-1': 'swap sides' },
              why: String.raw`Multiplying both sides by $\frac94$ cancels the $\frac49$ in front of $x^2$.` },
            { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Put $x^2$ into $V=\pi\int x^2\,\mathrm dy$`,
              from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^4 x^2\,\mathrm dy\qquad x^2=\T{s-1}{\frac{9y}{4}}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\int_0^4\T{s-1}{\frac{9y}{4}}\,\mathrm dy`, arrows: { 's-1': 'radius²' },
              why: String.raw`A disk of radius $x$ has area $\pi x^2$; the water fills $0 \le y \le 4$.` },
            { kind: 'calculus', label: String.raw`$\frac94$ out front, integrate $y$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{9\pi}{4}\T{s-2}{\Big[\frac{y^2}{2}\Big]_0^4}`, map: { 's-1': ['s-2'] },
              why: String.raw`The antiderivative of $y$ is $\frac{y^2}{2}$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$\frac{16}{2} = 8$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{9\pi}{4}\cdot\T{s-3}{8}=18\pi\approx 56.5\text{ dm}^3`, map: { 's-2': ['s-3'] },
              why: String.raw`Exactly half of the cylinder around the bowl, $\pi\cdot 9\cdot 4 = 36\pi$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(b)', prompt: String.raw`Volume of water when the depth is $h$ (variable <code>h</code>):`, kind: 'expression', variable: 'h', answer: '9*pi*h.^2/8', domain: [0.3, 4], solution: String.raw`$V(h) = \pi\int_0^h \frac{9y}{4}\,\mathrm d y = \frac{9\pi h^2}{8}$.` },
        { label: '(c)', prompt: String.raw`Volume of the cap of height $h$ from the ball of radius $5$ (variable <code>h</code>):`, kind: 'expression', variable: 'h', answer: 'pi*h.^2.*(15 - h)/3', domain: [0.3, 9.7], solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>Slices perpendicular to the $y$-axis are disks of radius $\sqrt{25 - y^2}$; the cap runs from $y = 5 - h$ to the top $y = 5$. We integrate and simplify.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { up: 1, lo: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'calculus', label: 'Integrate term by term',
              from: String.raw`V=\pi\int_{5-h}^{5}\left(25-y^2\right)\mathrm dy`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\Big[25y-\frac{y^3}{3}\Big]_{5-h}^{5}`,
              why: String.raw`$25$ is a constant (antiderivative $25y$), and $y^2$ integrates to $\frac{y^3}{3}$.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`Insert $y = 5$ and $y = 5-h$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\left(\T{up-1}{\frac{250}{3}}-\T{lo-1}{\left(25(5-h)-\frac{(5-h)^3}{3}\right)}\right)`,
              why: String.raw`At $y = 5$: $125-\frac{125}{3}=\frac{250}{3}$. The lower limit stays as an expression in $h$ for now.` },
            { kind: 'expand', label: String.raw`Expand $(5-h)^3$ and combine over $3$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\left(\T{up-1}{\frac{250}{3}}-\T{lo-1}{\frac{250-15h^2+h^3}{3}}\right)`,
              why: String.raw`$(5-h)^3 = 125-75h+15h^2-h^3$ and $25(5-h)=\frac{375-75h}{3}$. Subtracting, the $h$ terms cancel: $\frac{375-75h-125+75h-15h^2+h^3}{3}$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$250$ cancels, factor out $h^2$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\pi\cdot\T{V-1}{\frac{15h^2-h^3}{3}}=\frac{\pi h^2(15-h)}{3}`, map: { 'up-1': ['V-1'], 'lo-1': ['V-1'] },
              why: String.raw`$\frac{250}{3}-\frac{250}{3}=0$, and subtracting the bracket flips the signs of $-15h^2$ and $h^3$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(d)', prompt: String.raw`Evaluate the cap volume for $h = 2$.`, kind: 'numeric', answer: '52*pi/3', solution: String.raw`$\frac{\pi\cdot 4\cdot 13}{3} = \frac{52\pi}{3}$.` },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'a3',
      title: 'Known cross-sections',
      difficulty: 'core',
      statement: String.raw`<p>The base of a solid is the region between $y = x^2$ and $y = 4$. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis have their base across the region (from $x = -\sqrt y$ to $x = \sqrt y$).</p>`,
      parts: [
        { label: '(a)', prompt: 'Volume if the cross-sections are squares:', kind: 'numeric', answer: '32', solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>At height $y$ the base runs from $x = -\sqrt y$ to $x = \sqrt y$, so the side of the square is $2\sqrt y$. We find the area of the square and integrate it over $0 \le y \le 4$.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { s: 1, A: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Put the side into $A = s^2$`,
              from: String.raw`A(y)=s^2\qquad s=\T{s-1}{2\sqrt y}`,
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\left(\T{s-1}{2\sqrt y}\right)^2`, arrows: { 's-1': 'side' },
              why: String.raw`Area of a square = side squared.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: 'Square both factors',
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\T{A-1}{4y}`, map: { 's-1': ['A-1'] },
              why: String.raw`$2^2 = 4$ and $(\sqrt y)^2 = y$.` },
            { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Add up the slices`,
              from: String.raw`V=\int_0^4 A(y)\,\mathrm dy\qquad A(y)=\T{A-1}{4y}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\int_0^4\T{A-1}{4y}\,\mathrm dy`, arrows: { 'A-1': 'slice area' },
              why: String.raw`The region reaches from $y = 0$ (vertex of the parabola) to $y = 4$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: 'Integrate',
              to: String.raw`V=\Big[\T{A-2}{2y^2}\Big]_0^4=32`, map: { 'A-1': ['A-2'] },
              why: String.raw`The antiderivative of $4y$ is $2y^2$, and $2\cdot 16 = 32$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(b)', prompt: 'Volume if the cross-sections are equilateral triangles:', kind: 'numeric', answer: '8*sqrt(3)', solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>The side of the triangle is again $2\sqrt y$, and an equilateral triangle of side $s$ has area $\frac{\sqrt3}{4}s^2$. We find the area and integrate it.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { s: 1, A: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the side into the triangle area',
              from: String.raw`A(y)=\frac{\sqrt3}{4}s^2\qquad s=\T{s-1}{2\sqrt y}`,
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\frac{\sqrt3}{4}\left(\T{s-1}{2\sqrt y}\right)^2`, arrows: { 's-1': 'side' },
              why: String.raw`Height of an equilateral triangle is $\frac{\sqrt3}{2}s$, so its area is $\frac12\cdot s\cdot\frac{\sqrt3}{2}s$.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$(2\sqrt y)^2 = 4y$, and $\frac{4}{4} = 1$`,
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\T{A-1}{\sqrt3\,y}`, map: { 's-1': ['A-1'] },
              why: String.raw`The $4$ from squaring cancels the $4$ in the denominator.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: 'Integrate over 0 ≤ y ≤ 4',
              from: String.raw`V=\int_0^4\T{A-1}{\sqrt3\,y}\,\mathrm dy`,
              to: String.raw`V=\sqrt3\Big[\T{A-2}{\frac{y^2}{2}}\Big]_0^4=\sqrt3\cdot 8=8\sqrt3`, map: { 'A-1': ['A-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$\sqrt3$ is a constant; $\frac{16}{2} = 8$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(c)', prompt: 'Volume if the cross-sections are semicircles:', kind: 'numeric', answer: '4*pi', solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>The diameter of the semicircle is the base $2\sqrt y$, so its radius is $\sqrt y$. A semicircle has half the area of a disk. We find the area and integrate it.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { rad: 1, A: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the radius into the semicircle area',
              from: String.raw`A(y)=\frac12\pi\,\rho^2\qquad \rho=\T{rad-1}{\sqrt y}`,
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\frac12\pi\left(\T{rad-1}{\sqrt y}\right)^2`, arrows: { 'rad-1': 'radius' },
              why: String.raw`Half of the disk area $\pi\rho^2$.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$(\sqrt y)^2 = y$`,
              to: String.raw`A(y)=\T{A-1}{\frac{\pi y}{2}}`, map: { 'rad-1': ['A-1'] },
              why: String.raw`Squaring undoes the root for $y \ge 0$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: 'Integrate over 0 ≤ y ≤ 4',
              from: String.raw`V=\int_0^4\T{A-1}{\frac{\pi y}{2}}\,\mathrm dy`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{\pi}{2}\Big[\T{A-2}{\frac{y^2}{2}}\Big]_0^4=\frac{\pi}{2}\cdot 8=4\pi`, map: { 'A-1': ['A-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$\frac{\pi}{2}$ is a constant; $\frac{16}{2} = 8$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'a4',
      title: 'A ring by shells',
      difficulty: 'core',
      hw: 'HW1-style',
      statement: String.raw`<p>The region between $y = 0$ and $y = 1 - (x - 3)^2$ (so $2 \le x \le 4$) is rotated about the $y$-axis, giving a ring.</p>`,
      parts: [
        { label: '(a)', prompt: 'Which integral gives the volume?', kind: 'choice', choices: [String.raw`$2\pi\int_2^4 x\left(1 - (x-3)^2\right)\mathrm d x$`, String.raw`$\pi\int_2^4 \left(1 - (x-3)^2\right)^2\mathrm d x$`, String.raw`$2\pi\int_2^4 \left(1 - (x-3)^2\right)\mathrm d x$`, String.raw`$2\pi\int_{-1}^{1} x\left(1 - x^2\right)\mathrm d x$`], answer: 0, solution: String.raw`Shells: radius $x$, height $1 - (x-3)^2$. Option 4 forgot to shift the radius after substituting $s = x - 3$.` },
        { label: '(b)', prompt: 'Compute the volume.', kind: 'numeric', answer: '8*pi', hint: String.raw`Substitute $s = x - 3$; the odd part vanishes.`, solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>We shift the variable to the centre of the cross-section, $s = x - 3$: then $x = s + 3$, $\mathrm dx = \mathrm ds$, and the limits $x = 2, 4$ become $s = -1, 1$. The odd part of the integrand then vanishes.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { x: 1, xs: 2, o: 3, e: 4 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: String.raw`Substitute $s = x - 3$`,
              from: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_2^4 \T{x-1}{x}\left(1-\left(\T{xs-1}{x-3}\right)^2\right)\mathrm dx`,
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_{-1}^{1}\T{x-1}{(s+3)}\left(1-\T{xs-1}{s}^2\right)\mathrm ds`, arrows: { 'x-1': 'x = s + 3', 'xs-1': 'x − 3 = s' },
              why: String.raw`The radius is still $x$, now written as $s+3$. The limits move with the variable: $x=2 \Rightarrow s=-1$, $x=4 \Rightarrow s=1$.` },
            { kind: 'expand', label: String.raw`Split $(s+3)$ into two integrals`,
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_{-1}^{1}\T{o-1}{s\left(1-s^2\right)}\,\mathrm ds+2\pi\int_{-1}^{1}\T{e-1}{3\left(1-s^2\right)}\,\mathrm ds`, map: { 'x-1': ['o-1', 'e-1'], 'xs-1': ['o-1', 'e-1'] }, arrows: { 'x-1': 's and 3 separately' },
              why: String.raw`Multiply each part of $s+3$ by the bracket; an integral of a sum is the sum of the integrals.` },
            { kind: 'cancel', label: 'Odd integrand on [−1, 1] gives 0',
              to: String.raw`V=2\pi\int_{-1}^{1}\T{e-1}{3\left(1-s^2\right)}\,\mathrm ds`,
              why: String.raw`$s(1-s^2)$ changes sign when $s$ does, so the areas left and right of $0$ cancel exactly.` },
            { kind: 'calculus', label: String.raw`$3$ out front, integrate`,
              to: String.raw`V=6\pi\T{e-2}{\Big[s-\frac{s^3}{3}\Big]_{-1}^{1}}`, map: { 'e-1': ['e-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$2\pi\cdot 3 = 6\pi$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$\frac23-\left(-\frac23\right)=\frac43$`,
              to: String.raw`V=6\pi\cdot\T{e-3}{\frac43}=8\pi`, map: { 'e-2': ['e-3'] },
              why: String.raw`At $s=1$: $1-\frac13=\frac23$; at $s=-1$: $-\frac23$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(c)', prompt: String.raw`The same cross-section is moved so that its centre is at $x = 6$ (region between $y = 0$ and $y = 1 - (x-6)^2$). Volume of the new ring?`, kind: 'numeric', answer: '16*pi', solution: String.raw`The same computation gives $2\pi\cdot 6\cdot\frac43 = 16\pi$: the volume is the area $\frac43$ times the distance $2\pi\cdot 6$ travelled by the centroid (Pappus).` },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'a5',
      title: 'Write-up: the napkin ring',
      difficulty: 'exam',
      hw: 'HW1-style',
      statement: String.raw`<p>A cylindrical hole of radius $a$ is drilled along a diameter of a ball of radius $R > a$. Show with the shell method that the remaining ring has volume $V = \frac{4\pi}{3}\left(R^2 - a^2\right)^{3/2}$, and express it through the height $h = 2\sqrt{R^2 - a^2}$ of the ring. Write the derivation as a Live Script with a numerical check and a plot of the generating region.</p>`,
      parts: [
        { label: '(a)', prompt: String.raw`Volume for $R = 5$, $a = 3$:`, kind: 'numeric', answer: '256*pi/3', solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>We put $R = 5$ and $a = 3$ into the ring formula and simplify.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { R: 1, a: 2, p: 3 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put the given values into the formula',
              from: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\left(\T{R-x}{R}^2-\T{a-x}{a}^2\right)^{3/2}\qquad R=\T{R-1}{5},\quad a=\T{a-1}{3}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\left(\T{R-1}{5}^2-\T{a-1}{3}^2\right)^{3/2}`, arrows: { 'R-1': 'R = 5', 'a-1': 'a = 3' },
              why: String.raw`Each number keeps the colour of the letter it replaces.` },
            { kind: 'calc', label: String.raw`$25 - 9 = 16$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\cdot\T{p-1}{16}^{3/2}`, map: { 'R-1': ['p-1'], 'a-1': ['p-1'] },
              why: String.raw`Work out the bracket before the power.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$16^{3/2} = (\sqrt{16})^3 = 64$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\cdot\T{p-2}{64}=\frac{256\pi}{3}`, map: { 'p-1': ['p-2'] },
              why: String.raw`The power $\frac32$ means: square root, then cube. $\sqrt{16}=4$ and $4^3=64$.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(b)', prompt: String.raw`In terms of the height $h$ of the ring, $V = \;?$`, kind: 'choice', choices: [String.raw`$\frac{\pi h^3}{6}$`, String.raw`$\frac{\pi h^3}{3}$`, String.raw`$\frac{4\pi h^3}{3}$`, String.raw`$\pi h^2 R$`], answer: 0, solution: [
          { type: 'text', html: String.raw`<p>We solve the height formula for the root, raise it to the power $3$, and substitute into the volume.</p>` },
          { type: 'derive', colors: { h: 1, w: 2 }, steps: [
            { kind: 'both', label: String.raw`Both sides $\div 2$`,
              from: String.raw`\T{h-1}{h}=2\,\T{w-1}{\sqrt{R^2-a^2}}`,
              to: String.raw`\T{w-1}{\sqrt{R^2-a^2}}=\frac{\T{h-1}{h}}{2}`, arrows: { 'h-1': '÷ 2, swap sides', 'w-1': '' },
              why: String.raw`Dividing both sides by $2$ frees the root.` },
            { kind: 'both', label: 'Both sides to the power 3',
              to: String.raw`\T{w-2}{\left(R^2-a^2\right)^{3/2}}=\T{h-2}{\frac{h^3}{8}}`, map: { 'w-1': ['w-2'], 'h-1': ['h-2'] },
              why: String.raw`$(\sqrt{w})^3 = w^{3/2}$ and $\left(\frac h2\right)^3=\frac{h^3}{8}$. Doing the same to both sides keeps them equal.` },
            { kind: 'sub', label: 'Put it into the volume',
              from: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\left(R^2-a^2\right)^{3/2}\qquad \left(R^2-a^2\right)^{3/2}=\T{h-2}{\frac{h^3}{8}}`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{4\pi}{3}\cdot\T{h-2}{\frac{h^3}{8}}`, arrows: { 'h-2': 'replace' },
              why: String.raw`The whole power is replaced by the expression in $h$.` },
            { kind: 'result', label: String.raw`$\frac{4}{3\cdot 8} = \frac16$`,
              to: String.raw`V=\frac{\pi\,\T{h-3}{h^3}}{6}`, map: { 'h-2': ['h-3'] },
              why: String.raw`$R$ has disappeared: every ring of height $h$ has the same volume, whatever the size of the ball.` },
          ] },
        ] },
        { label: '(c)', prompt: 'Write the derivation in Live Script style and compare with the model solution.', kind: 'writeup' },
      ],
      writeup: true,
      writeupTemplate: [
        { type: 'heading', content: 'Problem 5 (Attempted)' },
        { type: 'text', content: 'We place the centre of the ball at the origin and the hole along the $y$-axis ...' },
        { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`V = 2\pi \int_a^R ` },
      ],
      solution: [
        { type: 'heading', content: 'Problem 5 (Attempted)' },
        { type: 'text', content: 'We place the centre of the ball at the origin and drill the hole along the $y$-axis. The ring is generated by rotating about the $y$-axis the region $a \\le x \\le R$, $-\\sqrt{R^2 - x^2} \\le y \\le \\sqrt{R^2 - x^2}$. A vertical strip at $x$ sweeps out a shell of radius $x$ and height' },
        { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`h(x) = 2\sqrt{R^2 - x^2}.` },
        { type: 'text', content: 'The shell method gives' },
        { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`V = 2\pi \int_a^R x \cdot 2\sqrt{R^2 - x^2}\,\mathrm d x .` },
        { type: 'text', content: 'We substitute $u = R^2 - x^2$, $\\mathrm d u = -2x\\,\\mathrm d x$; the limits $x = a, R$ become $u = R^2 - a^2, 0$:' },
        { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`V = 2\pi \int_0^{R^2 - a^2} u^{1/2}\,\mathrm d u = 2\pi \Big[ \frac23 u^{3/2} \Big]_0^{R^2 - a^2} = \frac{4\pi}{3}\left(R^2 - a^2\right)^{3/2}.` },
        { type: 'text', content: 'The height of the ring is $h = 2\\sqrt{R^2 - a^2}$, so $(R^2 - a^2)^{3/2} = h^3/8$ and' },
        { type: 'equation', content: String.raw`V = \frac{\pi h^3}{6},` },
        { type: 'text', content: 'which does not depend on $R$. We check the formula for $R = 5$, $a = 3$ and plot the generating region:' },
        { type: 'code', content: "R = 5; a = 3;\nV = 2*pi*integral(@(x) x.*2.*sqrt(R^2 - x.^2), a, R)\nVformula = 4*pi/3*(R^2 - a^2)^(3/2)\nx = linspace(a, R, 200);\nfill([x fliplr(x)], [sqrt(R^2 - x.^2) fliplr(-sqrt(R^2 - x.^2))], [0.75 0.85 1])\nhold on\nxline(0, 'k--')          % axis of rotation\naxis equal; grid on\ntitle('Generating region of the ring')" },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
